FG-DUCS artifact: license scope

This is a collection of materials with different origins, not a grant of one
license over the entire MTSA codebase or its dependency bundle.

The MIT License below applies to the original standalone FG-DUCS replication
scripts and their newly written documentation: fetch_assets.py,
check_package.py, reproduce_validation.py; the rq3_xeon campaign/collection/
rendering and PowerShell scripts; experiments/paper_witnesses/check_witnesses.py; and the standalone
experiments/legacy_fidelity adapter, orchestration, collection and preparation code.
It does not relicense MTSA-derived Java, inherited benchmark models, paper PDFs,
third-party libraries, or software contained in any shaded JAR. Their applicable
upstream terms and the dependency findings are described in NOTICE. The authors
have confirmed redistribution permission for the MTSA-derived sources; existing
individual source headers remain in force. Third-party JARs are not distributed.

